MastiFore — System Architecture & Workflow
1. System Architecture Overview

MastiFore is a multimodal AI-driven cattle health monitoring system designed for the early screening and risk stratification of bovine mastitis.

The system combines animal identification, milk-quality parameters, behavioural indicators, computer vision, thermal imaging, and temporal analysis rather than relying on a single diagnostic parameter.

The architecture follows this pipeline:

Animal → Data Acquisition → Preprocessing → Modality-Specific AI → Multimodal Fusion → Three-Tier Decision Engine → Alert & Visualization → Veterinary Validation → Feedback

The system is designed as a closed-loop decision-support platform. AI identifies abnormal patterns and estimates risk, while veterinary examination remains the final validation step.

